WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:12.440
This video shows how to put an animation from Pixodesk SVG Animator into an Astro site, as a single SVG file. There is no library, and nothing to install.

2
00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.730
Let's start with the site as it is.

3
00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:22.218
A heading, and nothing that moves yet.

4
00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:29.423
The animation comes first. Let's switch to the editor, where a football is already drawn.

5
00:00:30.967 --> 00:00:33.553
It's a vector drawing, standing still.

6
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.464
To make it move, let's switch on Auto mode.

7
00:00:39.967 --> 00:00:43.598
With Auto mode on, every change becomes a keyframe.

8
00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:48.020
Half a second in, let's drag the ball down to the floor.

9
00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:54.869
A keyframe appears on the timeline, holding the new position.

10
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.033
At one second, let's bring it back up.

11
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:04.677
Now it falls and rises again, in one second.

12
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:12.849
A real ball speeds up as it falls, and slows down as it rises. Let's set that easing.

13
00:01:19.967 --> 00:01:24.512
Gravity easing, falling and rising, makes the bounce feel natural.

14
00:01:25.733 --> 00:01:29.234
One bounce is not enough, so let's loop the animation.

15
00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.853
Loop is saved with the file, so the animation repeats forever.

16
00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:44.918
The animation is ready. Let's save it as SVG, into the project's assets.

17
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:56.091
The animation is written into the SVG file itself, as CSS.

18
00:01:57.333 --> 00:01:59.580
Now, back to our page.

19
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.600
The SVG file is already there, in the assets folder.

20
00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:09.281
Let's import the SVG file, as text.

21
00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.431
The raw suffix gives us the file's markup, as a string.

22
00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:22.357
Then, let's put that markup into the page.

23
00:02:28.733 --> 00:02:36.230
Set HTML inlines the SVG when the site is built, so its animation runs right in the page.

24
00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:40.131
Let's reload the page, and watch.

25
00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:50.361
There it is. The ball bounces, and the page loads no player at all.

26
00:02:52.400 --> 00:03:00.393
So, one SVG file saved from the editor, inlined when the site is built. That's all it takes, with no library at all.
